# UI Spec (`apps/ui-spec`)

**Do not use Figma** for UI design or frontend implementation in this repo. The canonical UI constraint library is `apps/ui-spec`.

## Mandatory: reference component examples

Before designing or implementing **any** portal page, screen, or shared UI component:

1. Open `apps/ui-spec/src/app/page.tsx` — find the **closest matching showcase example** (forms, tables, dialogs, auth cards, sidebar layouts, empty states, etc.).
2. Open the corresponding primitive in `apps/ui-spec/src/components/ui/<name>.tsx` — match props, variants, and composition.
3. Implement in `packages/ui` or portal apps by **mirroring** that example; do not invent one-off patterns.

Run the showcase locally when unsure:

```bash
rtk pnpm --filter @meridian/ui-spec dev
# http://localhost:<ui-spec-port>
```

In design docs and PR descriptions, cite the ui-spec reference, e.g. `Table + Badge` from `apps/ui-spec/src/app/page.tsx`, or `Dialog` pattern from `alert-dialog` section.

## When to read

Before designing screens (`ui-designer`) or implementing UI (`nextjs-frontend`), read:

1. `apps/ui-spec/README.md` — overview and agent workflow
2. `apps/ui-spec/src/app/page.tsx` — **component showcase (primary reference)**
3. `apps/ui-spec/src/app/globals.css` — design tokens (colors, radius, sidebar)
4. `apps/ui-spec/components.json` — shadcn style (`base-nova`), icon library (`lucide`)
5. `apps/ui-spec/src/components/ui/*.tsx` — allowed primitives and their APIs

## Rules

- **Components:** Only use primitives defined in `apps/ui-spec/src/components/ui/`. Map to `packages/ui` or app `components/ui/` — keep APIs aligned with ui-spec.
- **Composition:** Copy structure from showcase examples (spacing, variants, nested layout). ERP pages are not marketing landings — prefer data-dense patterns shown in ui-spec.
- **Tokens:** Match CSS variables from `apps/ui-spec/src/app/globals.css`. Do not invent one-off hex colors.
- **Variants:** Follow showcase usage in `page.tsx` (Button, Badge, Table, Dialog, Sheet, etc.).
- **Icons:** `lucide-react` per ui-spec `components.json` (portals may use `@tabler/icons-react` in shells only if already established in `packages/ui`).
- **New patterns:** If a screen needs a primitive or composition not in ui-spec, **add the example to ui-spec first**, then propagate to `packages/ui` and portal apps.
- **No Figma MCP:** Do not call Figma tools, sync to Figma, or block on Figma node IDs.

## Portal implementation

| Layer | Location |
|-------|----------|
| Spec (source + examples) | `apps/ui-spec/` |
| Shared shells & composites | `packages/ui/` |
| App routes & feature UI | `apps/admin/`, `apps/merchant/`, `apps/store/` |
| Screen wireframes | `docs/design/<feature>.md` |

Design docs describe layout and behavior; **visual and compositional constraints come from ui-spec showcase examples**.
